### 3. Add a Safety Net for the Async Thread
**File:** JournalBulkValidationService.java
**Method:** processAsync
Currently, java.lang.Error exceptions (like NoSuchMethodError or OutOfMemoryError) bypass your catch blocks and kill the thread instantly. This leaves the batch stuck in PROCESSING forever. You must catch Throwable to guarantee the database status updates to ERROR if the JVM panics.
**Add this catch block right before your finally block:**
```java
        } catch (NullPointerException | ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException e) {
